  "title": "UK Asylum Seekers Given New Guidance on Consent, Equality and Sexual Offences",
  "summary": "A new Home Office information booklet issued to asylum seekers in the UK has drawn attention for its detailed guidance on sexual consent, gender equality, domestic abuse and behaviour in public spaces. The guidance is intended to explain important aspects of British law and social expectations to people arriving in the country. According to reporting by The Sun, the resource contains several pages explaining that sexual activity must involve consent, that children cannot legally consent to sex",
